a)IMPLICIT ANIMATION: 
Implicit animations in Flutter are a simple way to add animation effects to user 
  interface elements. They automatically animate changes in a widget's properties,
  such as size, color, position, opacity, padding, and alignment.
Flutter provides special widgets such as AnimatedContainer, AnimatedOpacity, 
  AnimatedPadding, AnimatedAlign, AnimatedPositioned, AnimatedScale, and AnimatedRotation.
  These widgets automatically detect changes in their properties and animate from the 
  old value to the new value. When a value changes inside setState(), Flutter automatically
  creates the transition. The duration property specifies how long the animation should take, 
  while the curve property controls the style or speed of the animation.
1. AnimatedContainer
  AnimatedContainer is used to animate changes in properties such as width, height, color, padding, and border radius.
2. AnimatedOpacity
  AnimatedOpacity is used to create fade-in and fade-out effects.
3. AnimatedPadding
  AnimatedPadding smoothly changes the padding around a widget.
4. AnimatedAlign
  AnimatedAlign is used to smoothly move a widget from one alignment to another.
5. AnimatedScale
  AnimatedScale is used to increase or decrease the size of a widget.


